00:21:21.562 --> 00:21:23.237
- Here's a KISSmetrics story.

00:21:23.237 --> 00:21:25.888
Four years ago, which
is roughly one share,

00:21:25.888 --> 00:21:27.181
maybe a bit more than that now.

00:21:27.181 --> 00:21:28.536
I think we're up four and a half,

00:21:28.536 --> 00:21:30.873
we took a million dollars in seed funding

00:21:30.873 --> 00:21:33.142
from some angel investors.

00:21:33.142 --> 00:21:34.947
We created a version with that.

00:21:34.947 --> 00:21:36.960
It was called Version 1.0.

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:40.181
We were going to create a
better Google Analytics, right?

00:21:40.181 --> 00:21:42.294
Everyone use Google Analytics here?

00:21:42.294 --> 00:21:44.407
Probably have some issues
with Google Analytics, right,

00:21:44.407 --> 00:21:45.967
like, yeah, it could be better.

00:21:45.967 --> 00:21:47.361
Well, we were going to
create a better version of it

00:21:47.361 --> 00:21:49.198
and we were going to charge you for it.

00:21:49.198 --> 00:21:50.477
What was the issue?

00:21:50.477 --> 00:21:51.911
No one wanted it because they loved

00:21:51.911 --> 00:21:53.710
how Google Analytics was free.

00:21:53.710 --> 00:21:55.790
But I built it because I wanted it.

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:57.423
Terrible idea, right?

00:21:57.423 --> 00:21:58.911
Spent a year on that.

00:21:58.911 --> 00:22:01.560
Version 2, and at this point
we were running out of money,

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:03.084
so we had to raise another round.

00:22:03.084 --> 00:22:04.600
We raised three million bucks.

00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:06.770
Version 2, only took six months this time.

00:22:06.770 --> 00:22:08.328
Didn't take a year.

00:22:08.328 --> 00:22:11.766
We created a Facebook analytics company

00:22:11.766 --> 00:22:14.159
off of Dave Mcclure's AARRR metrics,

00:22:14.159 --> 00:22:16.031
you know, like the pirate, A-A-R-R-R,

00:22:16.031 --> 00:22:17.169
something like that.

00:22:17.169 --> 00:22:18.608
That didn't work out as well.

00:22:18.608 --> 00:22:21.389
We found out these
Facebook gaming companies

00:22:21.389 --> 00:22:22.813
actually don't make that much money

00:22:22.813 --> 00:22:24.844
or have a ton of money to spend on games.

00:22:24.844 --> 00:22:25.790
Don't believe me?

00:22:25.790 --> 00:22:27.248
Look at Zynga's stock, right?

00:22:27.248 --> 00:22:29.125
It's in the shitter, so.

00:22:29.125 --> 00:22:30.494
(laughing)

00:22:30.494 --> 00:22:31.424
It really is.

00:22:31.424 --> 00:22:32.653
These games last for, like, six months

00:22:32.653 --> 00:22:33.983
and then they go down.

00:22:33.983 --> 00:22:36.022
But that's who I was trying
to build a product for.

00:22:36.022 --> 00:22:38.050
Learned the hard way that
they have a ton of data

00:22:38.050 --> 00:22:39.524
which is costly to compute

00:22:39.524 --> 00:22:42.440
and they don't want to
spend much money at all.

00:22:42.440 --> 00:22:46.389
Version 3 took less
than 30 days to launch.

00:22:46.389 --> 00:22:47.415
Funny enough, that was the version

00:22:47.415 --> 00:22:48.759
that we actually currently have.

00:22:48.759 --> 00:22:50.123
We iterated on it,

00:22:50.123 --> 00:22:52.206
but it's the version that
people continually pay for

00:22:52.206 --> 00:22:54.753
and the business is thriving, right?

00:22:54.753 --> 00:22:56.360
Lessons learned from this?

00:22:56.360 --> 00:22:59.025
Create a minimal, viable product.

00:22:59.025 --> 00:23:01.642
It's Eric Ries', you know,

00:23:01.642 --> 00:23:03.125
like, preaching his whole thing,

00:23:03.125 --> 00:23:05.359
MVP, Lean Startup, great book.

00:23:05.359 --> 00:23:06.657
Funny enough, he's been an advisor

00:23:06.657 --> 00:23:08.390
to our company from day one,

00:23:08.390 --> 00:23:10.337
but it took us, like, a year
and a half to get there.

00:23:10.337 --> 00:23:11.775
I don't know why, but,

00:23:11.775 --> 00:23:13.318
you know, we learned the hard way.

00:23:13.318 --> 00:23:14.151
As you can see,

00:23:14.151 --> 00:23:14.984
I'm on the business side,

00:23:14.984 --> 00:23:16.386
not the engineering side,

00:23:16.386 --> 00:23:18.956
and my co-founder's also a business guy.

00:23:18.956 --> 00:23:21.533
So, but it's worked out.

00:23:21.533 --> 00:23:23.565
So when you release a product

00:23:23.565 --> 00:23:25.562
and you do the minimal viable product,

00:23:25.562 --> 00:23:27.663
what that is is you
get something out there

00:23:27.663 --> 00:23:29.674
as quick as possible and you get feedback.

00:23:29.674 --> 00:23:31.256
For example, when we want to launch

00:23:31.256 --> 00:23:33.076
a new feature or report,

00:23:33.076 --> 00:23:36.443
we actually survey people
and just get their input,

00:23:36.443 --> 00:23:38.639
and then we'll go create
wireframes and designs

00:23:38.639 --> 00:23:40.025
that are clickable.

00:23:40.025 --> 00:23:41.511
We won't even develop it,

00:23:41.511 --> 00:23:43.071
and be like, hey, what
do you think about this,

00:23:43.071 --> 00:23:44.131
and we'll put fake data in there,

00:23:44.131 --> 00:23:45.069
and people are like, oh cool,

00:23:45.069 --> 00:23:46.152
I like this, or I want to see this,

00:23:46.152 --> 00:23:48.120
or I wish I could do that, blah blah blah.

00:23:48.120 --> 00:23:50.948
We keep on iterating and
eventually we'll create a version

00:23:50.948 --> 00:23:52.965
that actually works and
let people test it out

00:23:52.965 --> 00:23:54.717
with their data and iterate more

00:23:54.717 --> 00:23:56.541
until we get product market fit,

00:23:56.541 --> 00:23:57.758
which means that people are saying

00:23:57.758 --> 00:24:00.103
I'm really satisfied with your product

00:24:00.103 --> 00:24:03.371
and I'd be devastated
if it no longer existed,

00:24:03.371 --> 00:24:06.232
which means that they'll talk
about your product a lot,

00:24:06.232 --> 00:24:08.190
the word of mouth marketing will spread,

00:24:08.190 --> 00:24:09.731
they'll be willing to pay a lot more,

00:24:09.731 --> 00:24:11.976
churn will decrease,
stuff like that, right?

00:24:11.976 --> 00:24:13.412
So go for product market fit.

00:24:13.412 --> 00:24:16.068
You can Google it to look at
the product market fit pyramid

00:24:16.068 --> 00:24:17.673
and how that works.

00:24:17.673 --> 00:24:19.603
And again, don't worry about perfection

00:24:19.603 --> 00:24:21.344
when you're doing all this kind of stuff.

00:24:21.344 --> 00:24:23.626
It just helps you get
out products much faster.

00:24:23.626 --> 00:24:25.963
People will drop off unless you give 'em

00:24:25.963 --> 00:24:28.189
a reason to stick around.

00:24:28.189 --> 00:24:31.140
So one of my buddies, Mike,

00:24:31.140 --> 00:24:32.456
we were talking and I'm like,

00:24:32.456 --> 00:24:34.372
what makes you stick around?

00:24:34.372 --> 00:24:35.563
And we were drinking beers,

00:24:35.563 --> 00:24:39.014
and he's like, those
virus checkers, right?

00:24:39.014 --> 00:24:43.333
He runs McAfee and Norton
on his computer all the time

00:24:43.333 --> 00:24:44.807
and it actually causes
him to stick around,

00:24:44.807 --> 00:24:46.756
'cause when it tells him there's a virus,

00:24:46.756 --> 00:24:48.562
he has to stay and find out what it is

00:24:48.562 --> 00:24:50.491
so he finishes the whole test.

00:24:50.491 --> 00:24:52.665
Why he gets viruses on his computer?

00:24:52.665 --> 00:24:54.559
That's a whole different issue, right?

00:24:54.559 --> 00:24:55.768
But he has that problem,

00:24:55.768 --> 00:24:58.196
so he's always sticking around for McAfee.

00:24:58.196 --> 00:25:00.181
So I decided to analyze people's websites

00:25:00.181 --> 00:25:02.422
and tell 'em that there's errors.

00:25:02.422 --> 00:25:04.686
As they progress, there's
more and more errors, right,

00:25:04.686 --> 00:25:06.720
assuming we find 'em.

00:25:06.720 --> 00:25:07.792
Instead of showing 'em the errors,

00:25:07.792 --> 00:25:10.791
I say put in your information, right?

00:25:10.791 --> 00:25:12.832
Got more people to put in information.

00:25:12.832 --> 00:25:14.165
Gave 'em a reason to stick around

00:25:14.165 --> 00:25:17.373
because there was like,
there's errors, right?

00:25:17.373 --> 00:25:20.932
63.5% increase in responses.

00:25:20.932 --> 00:25:22.144
We were collecting leads.

00:25:22.144 --> 00:25:24.149
So not only were we getting more leads,

00:25:24.149 --> 00:25:26.918
but we had a 63-plus percent increase

00:25:26.918 --> 00:25:29.024
in people actually following up

00:25:29.024 --> 00:25:31.483
because we were giving 'em
a reason to stick around.

00:25:31.483 --> 00:25:32.824
If you're an entrepreneur
and you're looking

00:25:32.824 --> 00:25:33.717
for aggressive growth,

00:25:33.717 --> 00:25:35.580
there's three things you need to do.

00:25:35.580 --> 00:25:37.558
One, you need to leverage
content marketing.

00:25:37.558 --> 00:25:40.112
Give away the best information out there.

00:25:40.112 --> 00:25:42.334
The information needs to be so good

00:25:42.334 --> 00:25:44.960
that your competitors
won't dare to copy you.

00:25:44.960 --> 00:25:49.174
Number two, you need to
create unique business deals.

00:25:49.174 --> 00:25:51.916
So everyone looks at marketing
as the best way to grow.

00:25:51.916 --> 00:25:53.642
I actually see it as business development

00:25:53.642 --> 00:25:54.963
is the best way to grow.

00:25:54.963 --> 00:25:57.219
If you can strike up interesting deals

00:25:57.219 --> 00:25:59.794
with other businesses that
already have a user base,

00:25:59.794 --> 00:26:03.960
you can quickly grow and expand
your user base really fast.

00:26:03.960 --> 00:26:05.835
For example, if I run a marketing company

00:26:05.835 --> 00:26:08.118
and I'm trying to get more business owners

00:26:08.118 --> 00:26:10.042
and websites to sign up to my stuff,

00:26:10.042 --> 00:26:11.683
GoDaddy's a perfect
company to partner with

00:26:11.683 --> 00:26:13.890
'cause they already have
millions of customers.

00:26:13.890 --> 00:26:17.006
The third tip I would say
is just working really hard,

00:26:17.006 --> 00:26:18.492
in which people want to grow,

00:26:18.492 --> 00:26:21.353
but they don't want to put in
the time and energy to grow.

00:26:21.353 --> 00:26:22.861
If you're not willing to put in the hours

00:26:22.861 --> 00:26:24.210
and keep at it relentlessly

00:26:24.210 --> 00:26:25.921
whether you fail or you succeed,

00:26:25.921 --> 00:26:27.823
you just can't stop no matter what.

